```python
def my_function(input):
    if isinstance(input, str):
        return input
    elif isinstance(input, int):
        return input
    else:
        return (None,)  # or any other default value
```

This way, you're explicitly telling the caller what type of object was passed in and what type they get back. It also makes your code more readable and easier to understand.
